// The second half of the genre plans (genres.js holds the first and the
// machinery: PLANS, rollGenre, genrePrompt). Same shape, same test
// (test/genres.test.js holds every engine, preset, scale, kit and step string
// here to the engine's own tables). Kept apart only for size.
//
// A plan with `eighths: true` is written a step to an EIGHTH note (every
// track at speed 0.5), which is what lets master swing land on the offbeat
// eighths: jazz, blues, bossa, salsa. Its step strings are then two bars
// each. `steps` is how long a plan's step strings are when a bar is not four
// beats (12: two bars of 3/4 in eighths, or one of 12/8), with `meter`.

const FOUR = "x...x...x...x...";
const BACK = "....X.......X...";
const OFF = "..x...x...x...x.";
const E8 = "x.x.x.x.x.x.x.x.";
const S16 = "xoxoxoxoxoxoxoxo";

